Subject: Raw Revision Source for the Cantor M2B Windows Sys Compile Probe Lock Contract

Captured: 2026-07-30
Conversation: cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
Source type: implementation-observed specification correction

Preserve this source separately from canonical and exploded specifications.

The 0.1 compile-probe authority required two things that Cargo cannot satisfy
together:

1. cantor_ecosystem must gain a direct cfg(windows) dependency on the already
   locked windows-sys 0.61.2 package.
2. Cargo.lock must remain byte-identical.

The first locked build stopped before compilation and reported that Cargo.lock
needed an update. The reason is structural: Cargo.lock records the dependency
edges of local workspace packages as well as registry package identities. The
registry package was already present, but cantor_ecosystem was not yet recorded
as its direct consumer.

No compile-probe implementation is retained from that failed attempt. No
Windows function was called.

Revise the contract to version 0.2:

- preserve the exact target-specific windows-sys declaration from 0.1;
- preserve the five no-call function-item checks, six structure layout checks,
  six information-class checks, read-only constant checks, deterministic
  in-memory fingerprint, and all effect prohibitions;
- permit Cargo.lock to change in exactly one semantic way: add the existing
  package name "windows-sys" to the dependency array of the local
  cantor_ecosystem package;
- require the registry package universe to remain 112 packages;
- require every registry package version, source, and checksum to remain
  unchanged;
- require windows-sys to remain exactly 0.61.2 with checksum
  ae137229bcbd6cdf0f7b80a31df61766145077ddf49416a728b02cb3921ff3fc;
- require the pre-change Cargo.lock SHA-256 to remain
  7b2e1e879e387ccff1cf1e04de4ace1d72eb006d1443192ab26629f0c3a884a5;
- require the modeled post-change Cargo.lock SHA-256 to be
  ff20148aa6ff3c2774d07d454bc900f4f81d5594bd8f8e49af2a43217b7ee73a;
- require the textual Cargo.lock diff to be exactly one added line,
  ` "windows-sys",`, in cantor_ecosystem's dependency array;
- prohibit additions, removals, upgrades, downgrades, source changes,
  checksum changes, or feature resolution outside the declared direct edge.

The model was produced in an isolated detached worktree from commit 7e72391 by
adding only the intended target dependency and running Cargo offline. Cargo
reported 112 packages and the expected direct feature tree. That model is
research evidence, not implementation authority.

The 0.1 canonical and exploded specifications remain immutably preserved in Git
commit eb15842 and are explicitly invalidated by commit 7e72391. Reprocessing
must issue a new satisfaction signature. It must not silently reuse the invalid
0.1 signature.
